BSD-3-Clause, following picoquic.

These patches are this project's own work, and every line of them modifies a file in
private-octopus/picoquic, which is BSD-3-Clause. A patch against BSD-3-Clause source
produces BSD-3-Clause source, so the terms are picoquic's rather than this repository's
root MIT, and the patches are offered under the same licence as the code they change.

That is also what the README already intends. It records the buffer-key-loading API as
following "picoquic's existing provider pattern" and both patch sets as candidates for
upstream pull requests; a contribution offered upstream is offered under upstream's
terms, and this file states outright what that plan assumed.

The full text is picoquic's, in thirdparty/picoquic/LICENSE, beside the code these
patches apply to. Copyright in the changes themselves is this project's.
